{
  "$comment": "The DGA token ledger, extracted from the Platforms Code Figma library by /dga-sync. Keys are the Figma variable paths verbatim — including the library's own typos ('Font Wieght', 'text-Ig') — because that path is what a finding quotes back to a designer. score.mjs reads these keys directly; renaming a field silently disables a check.",
  "synced": "2026-08-18",
  "$notes": [
    "Extracted by walking get_variable_defs over seven pages — Get Started, Buttons, Inline Alert, Text input, Card, UI Shell Nav Header, Tags — because this library has no separate Foundations page. Its tokens live as Figma variables bound to the components.",
    "SPOT-CHECK: Tags (12:539) was walked last as an independent cross-check against a page none of the ledger was built from. It confirmed 14 values verbatim — the family, Text md/sm/xs, the whole spacing scale, radius-sm, radius-full, border-neutral-secondary, text-oncolor-primary — and found two things the first six pages had missed: a 'Text 2xs' ramp step (10/14) and the entire Tag token family, both since added. Worth repeating on a fresh page at the next sync.",
    "EXCLUDED as contamination, not DGA tokens: 'var(--p-color-text)' #303030, 'var(--p-color-bg-surface)' #ffffff, 'var(--p-sapce-600)' 24, 'var(--p-sapce-1000)' 40 — all found on the Get Started page. The 'p-' prefix and the 'sapce' misspelling are Shopify Polaris's own, so these are leftovers from a paste into the documentation page. Admitting them would have taught the auditor that #303030 is a compliant text colour.",
    "Alpha-bearing tokens (#ffffff33, #0000001a) are kept at full 8-digit hex. score.mjs matches on the first 6 digits, so an alpha variant and its opaque twin both count as matched — acceptable, since the site extractor composites alpha against the real background before measuring.",
    "SYNC 2 — Foundations - Platforms Code (1392267405633663431), pages: FOUNDATIONS 2:2, Colors 2:3, Typography 2:4, Effect styles 2:5, Spacing/radius/grids 2:6. Merged into the Components Library ledger; nothing was dropped.",
    "CLOSED by Foundations: spacing-sm=6 (the flagged gap), Display lg 48/60, Text xl 20/30, the full 7-level elevation set (was 2), 4 backdrop-blur levels, container paddings and max-width (S2 now measurable), and border widths.",
    "STILL MISSING: Display md. The display ramp runs 60, 48, ?, 30, 24 — a step around 36 is implied but was not emitted by any of the four Foundations pages. Not invented.",
    "STILL MISSING: no dark-mode variable set on any Foundations page either, so C4 remains n/a. Motion tokens likewise absent — Platforms Code appears not to define them as variables.",
    "EXCLUDED as documentation swatches, not tokens: guide-container-do #abefc6 and guide-container-avoid #fecdca from the Spacing/radius/grids page — the green/red do-and-avoid annotation colours on the guidance frames. Same class of trap as the Polaris leftovers caught in sync 1.",
    "Six Gradient/Brand/* variables exist but return empty values through get_variable_defs, so gradients are not in the ledger and are not checked.",
    "CONFLICT — Text/text-primary: Components had #1b8354, Foundations says #0d121c — Foundations wins",
    "CONFLICT — Border/border-secondary: Components had #dba102, Foundations says #e5e7eb — Foundations wins",
    "CONFLICT — Button/button-background-neutral-default: Components had #f3f4f6, Foundations says #f9fafb — Foundations wins",
    "CONFLICT — radius-sm: 4 on Foundations/Effect-styles, Colors and throughout the Components Library; 6 on Foundations/Spacing-radius-grids. Both are in radius.scale so neither is scored as a violation, and the disagreement is the library's, not the extraction's.",
    "CONFLICT — Border/border-primary: #d2d6db on Foundations/Typography, #1b8354 on Foundations/Colors. Kept #d2d6db (the neutral reading, matching Border 2/border-primary); the brand green is available as Colors/Foreground/fg-brand-primary.",
    "CROSS-CHECK NOT POSSIBLE this pass: Foundations has five pages and four carry the variables the ledger needed; the fifth (FOUNDATIONS 2:2) is a cover and returned {}. So unlike sync 1 there was no page held back as an independent check. Do the cross-check on the Icons or Mobile Components pass instead.",
    "Icons - Platforms Code is DEFERRED by choice, not missing. The auditor passes --na I1 while tokens.icons.deferred is true, so the icon check leaves the denominator instead of being judged against a baseline that was never loaded.",
    "SYNC 3 — Mobile Components - Platforms Code (1392271796654597578), pages: Buttons 1:1183, Text input 954:19434, Card 11367:20133, UI Shell Tab Bar 8332:23832, Checkbox 954:11220 (held back as the cross-check).",
    "KEY FINDING — mobile component anatomy is IDENTICAL to desktop. Button padding (lg 16 / md 12 / sm 8, gap 4, radius 4), Card (gap 24, radius 16, shadow-md) and Text input (padding-end 16, radius 4, border #9da4ae) match the desktop file value for value. Platforms Code does not respecify components per viewport; what changes is the shell — Tab Bar, Navigation Bar and Splash Screen replace Nav Header, Table of Contents and Footer. So P1-P3 compare against one spec at any width, and the earlier worry that 375px captures were judged by the wrong ruler applies only to the shell components, not to buttons, cards or fields.",
    "CROSS-CHECK (Checkbox 954:11220, held back from the extraction) confirmed radius-xs 2 / sm 4 / full 9999, Text md 16/24, Text sm 14/20, spacing xs 4 / xl 16 / 5xl 40, border-disabled #9da4ae and background-disabled #e5e7eb. It also independently reported Text/text-primary as #0d121c, which corroborates resolving that conflict in Foundations favour over the Components Library #1b8354. New from it: the whole Controls/ family for checkbox, radio and switch.",
    "GAP — no minimum target-size token in any synced file; see a11y.$note. A4 therefore scores against the WCAG floor at every viewport."
  ],
